1
00:00:00,556 --> 00:00:04,306
Every message you send travels
across an open network.

2
00:00:04,926 --> 00:00:06,756
The Internet was built for sharing,

3
00:00:07,246 --> 00:00:08,156
not for hiding.

4
00:00:08,681 --> 00:00:11,231
So security must be engineered in.

5
00:00:12,889 --> 00:00:15,299
Computer security protects assets.

6
00:00:15,874 --> 00:00:19,044
Hardware, software,
data and documentation.

7
00:00:19,744 --> 00:00:22,454
It guards them from unauthorized access,

8
00:00:22,824 --> 00:00:23,474
misuse,

9
00:00:24,504 --> 00:00:25,574
disclosure, modification,

10
00:00:26,044 --> 00:00:28,294
destruction and denial of service.

11
00:00:30,022 --> 00:00:32,072
Three goals anchor everything.

12
00:00:32,567 --> 00:00:37,297
Confidentiality means only
authorized parties read the data.

13
00:00:37,752 --> 00:00:41,602
Integrity means the data stays
accurate and trustworthy.

14
00:00:42,227 --> 00:00:45,197
Availability means it is
there when you need it.

15
00:00:46,789 --> 00:00:48,519
A fourth goal is authenticity.

16
00:00:49,359 --> 00:00:52,829
It assures you that a
message or person is genuine.

17
00:00:53,424 --> 00:00:54,734
Not an impostor.

18
00:00:56,489 --> 00:00:58,339
Why do we need security now?

19
00:00:58,819 --> 00:01:00,189
Everything is connected.

20
00:01:00,939 --> 00:01:02,189
Attacks are sophisticated:

21
00:01:03,059 --> 00:01:05,629
malware, phishing, denial of service.

22
00:01:06,189 --> 00:01:07,819
Information has value:

23
00:01:08,449 --> 00:01:10,779
money, personal data, state secrets.

24
00:01:11,424 --> 00:01:12,934
And the law demands it.

25
00:01:14,556 --> 00:01:16,026
Threats come in three kinds.

26
00:01:16,721 --> 00:01:19,771
Human threats:
hackers and careless insiders.

27
00:01:20,481 --> 00:01:23,051
Natural threats: floods and fires.

28
00:01:23,701 --> 00:01:27,831
Environmental threats:
power failure or hardware failure.

29
00:01:29,522 --> 00:01:32,992
Picture a sender and a
receiver on an open channel.

30
00:01:33,517 --> 00:01:36,107
An attacker can quietly read the message.

31
00:01:36,647 --> 00:01:38,137
Or change it on the way.

32
00:01:38,677 --> 00:01:40,987
Security services answer both.

33
00:01:42,689 --> 00:01:45,759
This is the vocabulary
of the whole course.

34
00:01:46,214 --> 00:01:50,744
Confidentiality, integrity,
availability, authenticity.

35
00:01:51,169 --> 00:01:53,199
Attacks, services, mechanisms.

36
00:01:54,034 --> 00:01:55,924
Everything else builds on these.

